+++
title: Duat
description: Underworld in Egyptian mythology
hook: "The absolute punishment in ancient Egyptian thought was not torment but
  ceasing to exist: a heart heavier than the feather of Maat was eaten by
  Ammit, and the dead person was denied existence after death in the Duat."
standfirst: A concept in ancient Egyptian mythology involving death, the Duat
  is most often seen as a realm where people go after they die, and generally
  known best as a dark subterranean realm housing the deceased and a variety
  of deities, divided by twelve guarded gates that represent each hour of the
  night.
